        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-de97cc1c",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "San José, Costa Rica: city buildings surrounded by greenery"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_title:ca0a4d6daf445776",
      "field": "itinerary.title",
      "sourceTextSha256": "abfeb451f72c811ec3ec6fa6b43cf170d98041e2c5380c7844f2c1eaaa30bccd",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-de97cc1c",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "Doka Coffee Plantation, Poás Volcano, La Paz and Arenal"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a18f3b664ac2839ace9be02583f0a5e21f99f21cf9fde17752bc52681a58c46e",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-de97cc1c",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, you’ll head to the Doka Coffee Plantation.\n\nHere you’ll see how coffee is made, from growing and picking the cherries to processing and roasting the beans.\n\nYou can buy coffee at a good price on the plantation.\n\nAfter the coffee tour, you’ll continue to Poás Volcano National Park.\n\nAs you climb, you’ll notice changes in temperature and vegetation. Along the way you’ll pass coffee plantations, flower greenhouses and strawberry farms.\n\nAt Poás, you’ll see the main crater with its sulfurous fumaroles. Your guide will explain the volcano’s activity and the national park’s different ecosystems.\n\nNext you’ll visit La Paz Waterfall Gardens.\n\nYou’ll follow a forest trail to the waterfalls.\n\nThe park also has a hummingbird gallery, a serpentarium, a bird garden, a butterfly farm and a frog exhibit.\n\nAfter the visit, you’ll travel to the Arenal Volcano area.\n\nYou’ll stay at Arenal Paraiso Resort & Spa.\n\nBreakfast and lunch are included today."
    },
    {
